From 4be972e6a9a8662ad267f77fb84bcfc95472e674 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luc Ho <mastergambler09@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:03:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recover lost anonymous sessions and stop creating them on
 network errors

- userService: only create a new anonymous user when account.get() returns 401.
  Transient failures are retried, then throw SessionUnavailableError instead of
  silently orphaning the user's groups. Lost sessions are recorded in account
  prefs (previousUserIds) for recovery.
- my-groups: show a retry prompt on SessionUnavailableError.
- deleteCurrentSession: delete server session before clearing local storage.
- scripts/diagnose-groups.mjs: read-only DB diagnostics.
- scripts/merge-user.mjs: move memberships, created groups, calendar entries and
  chat from an old userId to the current one (dry run by default, backup + undo).
- userService tests: reset cache between tests, cover new behavior.
- .gitignore: env files and merge backups.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eipm2tW7HVgiqTrGTUxX8Q
